li='Decision panel | Cutoff: November 25, 2026, 6:34 a.m. CST (12:34 UTC)\n\n1. OpenAI protein-design study separates generation from lab validation\nPublished November 24, 2026. FACT: OpenAI reports protein structure and sequence design with GPT-6 models using reasoning and code. Laboratory work with Onava found evidence of binding across five targets; specialist models helped filter candidates and supply sequences in the testing workflow.\nIMPLICATION: Evaluate a general model’s proposed solution separately from specialist screening and independent validation; apply the same separation to financial research agents.\nUNCERTAINTY: Early research, not proof of an end-to-end specialist-free design process. Complete structure prediction remains a weakness, and binding is not clinical efficacy.\nhttps://openai.com/index/gpt-6-models-demonstrate-intrinsic-protein-design-capabilities/\n\n2. New PPO hedging paper tests transfer from simulation to SPX options\nSubmitted November 24; listed November 25, 2026. FACT: The preprint trains PPO to hedge price and volatility risk using an underlying and a longer-dated option. It evaluates transfer to historical SPX options, reporting improved hedging outcomes concentrated in high-volatility episodes.\nIMPLICATION: Test a two-instrument hedging environment against practitioner Delta and Delta-Vega baselines, with identical costs and independent risk limits.\nUNCERTAINTY: Unreplicated research. Historical tests use 2019–2022 data, quoted mid-price P&L and overlapping episodes; reported gains do not establish executable live performance or rehabilitate a rejected equity-allocation PPO strategy.\nhttps://arxiv.org/abs/2611.32790\n\n3. Nasdaq futures fall more than 2% before the inflation release\nNovember 25, 2026, 5:01 a.m. CST reported snapshot. FACT: Reuters reported Dow, S&P 500 and Nasdaq-100 E-mini futures down 0.76%, 1.44% and 2.38%, respectively, at 6:01 a.m. Eastern ahead of the inflation release.\nIMPLICATION: Treat the QQQ-sensitive premarket gap and the scheduled data release as separate execution-risk windows; require fresh quotes before sizing participation.\nUNCERTAINTY: Reported snapshot, not executable live prices, SPY/QQQ returns or a prediction of the cash close.\nhttps://www.reuters.com/business/nasdaq-futures-slide-over-2-fresh-us-tariff-concerns-inflation-data-focus-2026-11-25/\n\n4. GDP and October PCE arrive together at 7:30 a.m. CST\nScheduled November 25, 2026, 7:30 a.m. CST; results unknown at cutoff. FACT: BEA schedules third-quarter GDP’s second estimate and October Personal Income and Outlays for November 25 at 8:30 a.m. Eastern, equivalent to 7:30 a.m. Central.\nIMPLICATION: Freeze pre-release inputs and measure the data reaction separately from the opening auction; avoid training on revised GDP as if it were known earlier.\nUNCERTAINTY: A scheduled release, not published results or a forecast. Subsequent revisions and policy interpretation remain uncertain.\nhttps://www.bea.gov/news/2026/personal-income-and-outlays-september-2026\n\n5. Dell lifts its full-year outlook after record quarterly revenue\nAnnounced November 24, 2026; quarter ended October 30. FACT: Dell reported fiscal third-quarter revenue of 54.9 billion and raised fiscal 2027 revenue guidance from 192.0 billion to 202.0 billion, in U.S. dollars. It also reported a record AI backlog.\nIMPLICATION: Separate booked demand, shipments and cash conversion in AI-infrastructure analysis; strong guidance alone does not establish investment returns.\nUNCERTAINTY: Company-reported unaudited results and forward guidance. Backlog conversion depends on customer financing and deployment capacity; no stock-price reaction is inferred.\nhttps://www.dell.com/en-us/newsroom/announcements/dell-technologies-delivers-third-quarter-fiscal-2027-financial-results\n\nVOLATILITY / EXECUTION: High, medium confidence; Nov. 24 prior-close VIX 26.36 (Yahoo Finance). Reported futures snapshot 5:01 a.m. CST, not live. Today GDP/PCE 7:30 a.m.; cash open 8:30 a.m. CST. Thanksgiving closed; Friday cash ends noon CST. Spreads, depth, volume, funding and gamma unverified. Use staged limits and fresh quotes. Six factor returns unavailable: comparable publication-cleared closes and publication rights unresolved. Intended windows Nov. 23–24 and Oct. 27–Nov. 24; no rankings.\n\nMATLAB / DRL: Independent capital-preservation gates; net-cost rewards; purged walk-forward regime tests. Stress bid/ask execution and overlapping episodes. Align timetables, profile and preserve random streams. Check leakage, survivorship, look-ahead, corporate actions, stale options quotes, multiple testing, calibration and drift.\n\nRESEARCH QUESTION: Does a simulated PPO Delta-Vega hedge retain lower tail loss with executable bid/ask prices, partial fills and independent regimes? Mid-price and overlapping-episode assumptions could change the answer.\n\nFull dashboard and five graphics: https://github.com/rsh63/market-state-lab/blob/main/2026-11-25.md\n\nResearch and education, not individualized financial advice.\n\nWhich execution stress would you test first: full bid/ask crossing or partial fills?\nEmail subscription: https://market-state-lab.ghost.io/?utm_source=linkedin&utm_medium=social&utm_campaign=qmb_2026-11-25#/portal/signup'

